RULED 2026-09-04 21:05:59 AUSEST (delegated by Mike; operator-reversible; full ruling, reviewer positions and implementation guidance in the NOTES, read them before briefing). This bead began as an operator call surfaced by rf2-l1hh: is the React Fiber-walker still the primary runtime view-hierarchy capture path that spec/View-Hierarchy-Capture.md (a v1 MUST for React-backed ports, locked 2026-05-19) requires? Answer: NO. Hierarchy capture is tool-owned and optional; the data-rf-view tag that 006 section View tagging contract already requires is the whole capture surface and stays a MUST because it has live consumers (Xray hover-highlight, Pair ui/read forward and reverse lookups).

THE WORK (one worker, one PR, hot-zone sequenced; details and line numbers in the RULING note, items A-G):
- delete spec/View-Hierarchy-Capture.md and its index/ownership rows (spec/README.md, spec/Ownership.md);
- rewrite spec/006-ReactiveSubstrate.md section View tagging contract: drop the (fallback) qualifier from the heading and update all anchor referrers (006, 011-SSR, Ownership, README, Spec-Schemas x2, Tool-Pair, skills/re-frame2-pair/references/screen-reads.md), replace the fallback/primary/coexist status note, keep the edge cases as known limits, replace the Walker contract subsection with a short optional tool-side Hierarchy inference subsection (nearest tagged ancestor rule), add a dated decision note naming this bead and commits fe4ff001b9, 9781aa4e24, da39b0c0f8;
- correct spec/Spec-Schemas.md :rf/view-id-attr status and prose, spec/Tool-Pair.md:446, spec/011-SSR.md:318;
- remove the walker MUST from skills/re-frame2-implementor (SKILL.md:75, references/phase-2-impl-order.md:36 and :61);
- delete the unwired tools/xray/src/day8/re_frame2_xray/views/view_walker.cljs and tools/xray/test/day8/re_frame2_xray/views/view_walker_dom_cljs_test.cljs (no caller at tip; test discovery is by regex, no build config change);
- correct the Fiber-primary wording in core docstrings (spine.cljs, source_coord_annotation.cljs, source_coords.cljc and its test), implementation/scripts/check-elision.cjs comments, the reagent and reagent-slim view-id-attr test docstrings, and the Pair preload runtime docstrings that cite the deleted walker.

GATES BY PATH: scripts/check_doc_slugs.py; mkdocs build --strict; npm run test:cljs (implementation/); npm run test:xray-feature-gate. Hand-verify table columns and the anchor referrer list; state in the PR body that tools/xray/spec is unchanged and why.

HISTORY CARRIED FORWARD: the walker was BUILT at fe4ff001b9 (PR #1533, 2026-05-19, under tools/causa/) and RETIRED at 9781aa4e24 (PR #1741, 2026-05-20) with the group-by-tree renderer, the views_view.cljs toggle, the React-version smoke and the __rf2_view_id__ property; the data-rf-view path landed at da39b0c0f8 (PR #1780) five hours after that deletion, so the two never coexisted. The contract bound ports, not the reference, so the reference's absence was never a violation; the cost was recurring drift on the carriers (rf2-l1hh, rf2-rn3u, rf2-amz1, rf2-cu5h in 48 hours). Follow-up: rf2-c5w1 (Hicasso carries neither dev-mode DOM annotation) lands after this PR.
